{
  "title": "Namaz of Imam al-Husayn (a.s.)",
  "data": "Upon concluding the prayer, say the following supplication:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَنْتَ الَّذِيْ اسْتَجَبْتَ لِاٰدَمَ وَحَوَّاءَ اِذْ قَالَا\nALLAAHUMMA ANTAL LADHEES TAJABTA LI-AADAMA WA HAWWAA'A IDH QAALAA\nO Allah, it is You who responded to Adam and Eve when they both said,\nرَبَّنَا ظَلَمْنَا اَنْفُسَنَا\nRABBANAA ZALAMNAA ANFUSANAA\n“Our Lord! We have been unjust to ourselves,\nوَاِنْ لَمْ تَغْفِرْ لَنَا وَتَرْحَمْنَا\nWA IN LAM TAGHFIR LANAA WA TARHAMNAA\nand if You forgive us not and have not mercy on us,\nلَنَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْخَاسِرِيْنَ\nLANAKOONANNA MINAL KHAASIREEN\nwe shall certainly be of the losers.”\nوَنَادَاكَ نُوْحٌ فَاسْتَجَبْتَ لَهٗ\nWA NAADAAKA NOOHUN FASTAJABTA LAHOO\nAnd when Noah cried to You, You answered him\nوَنَجَّيْتَهٗ وَاَهْلَهٗ مِنَ الكَرْبِ الْعَظِيْمِ\nWA NAJJAYTAHOO WA AHLAHOO MINAL KARBIL A'ZEEM\nand delivered him and his family from the great calamity.\nوَاَطْفَاْتَ نَارَ نُمْرُوْدَ عَنْ خَلِيْلِكَ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ\nWA ATFA'TA NAARA NUMROODA A'N KHALEELIKA IBRAAHEEM\nAnd it is You who extinguished the fire of Nimrod for Your intimate friend Abraham\nفَجَعَلْتَهَا بَرْداً وَسَلاماً\nFAJA'ALTAHAA BARDAN WA SALAAMAA\nand thus changed it into coldness and peace.\nوَاَنْتَ الَّذِيْ اسْتَجَبْتَ لِاَيُّوْبَ اِذْ نَادٰى\nWA ANTAL LADHEES TAJABTA LI-AYYOOBA IDH NAADAA\nAnd it is You Who responded to Job when he cried to You, saying,\nاِنِّيْ مَسَّنِيَ الضُّرُّ وَاَنْتَ اَرْحَمُ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nINNEE MASSANIYAD DURRU WA ANTA ARHAMUR RAAHIMEEN\n“Harm has afflicted me, and You are the most Merciful of all those who show mercy.”\nفَكَشَفْتَ مَا بِهٖ مِنْ ضُرٍّ\nFAKASHAFTA MAA BIHEE MIN DURR\nTherefore, You took off what harm he had,\nوَآتَيْتَهٗ اَهْلَهٗ وَمِثْلَهُمْ مَعَهُمْ\nWA AATAYTAHOO AHLAHOO WA MITHLAHUM MA'AHUM\nand You gave him his family and the like of them with them:\nرَحْمَةً مِنْ عِنْدِكَ وَذِكْرٰى لِاُوْلِيْ الْاَلْبَابِ\nRAHMATAN MIN I'NDIKA WA DHIKRAA LI-ULIL ALBAAB\na mercy from You and a reminder to the owners of sound intellects.\nوَاَنْتَ الَّذِيْ اسْتَجَبْتَ لِذِيْ النُّوْنِ\nWA ANTAL LADHEES TAJABTA LIDHIN NOON\nAnd it is You Who responded to Dhu'l-Nun (i.e. Prophet Jonah)\nحِيْنَ نَادَاكَ فِيْ الظّلُمَاتِ\nHEENA NAADAAKA FIZ ZULUMAAT\nwhen he cried through the depths of darkness,\nاَنْ لَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ سُبْحَانَكَ\nAN LAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANTA SUBHAANAKA\n“There is no god but You. Glory be to You.\nاِنِّيْ كُنْتُ مِنَ الظَّالِمِيْنَ\nINNEE KUNTU MINAZ ZAALIMEEN\nI was indeed of those who are wrong!”\nفَنَجَّيْتَهٗ مِنَ الغَمِّ\nFANAJJAYTAHOO MINAL GHAMM\nSo, You delivered him from distress.\nوَاَنْتَ الَّذِيْ اسْتَجَبْتَ لِمُوْسٰى وَهَارُوْنَ دَعْوَتَهُمَا\nWA ANTAL LADHEES TAJABTA LIMOOSAA WA HAAROONA DA'WATAHUMAA\nAnd it is You Who responded to the prayer of Moses and Aaron\nحِيْنَ قُلْتَ قَدْ اُجِيْبَتْ دَعْوَتُكُمَا فَاسْتَقِيْمَا\nHEENA QULTA QAD UJEEBAT DA'WATUKUMAA FASTAQEEMAA\nwhen You said, “Accepted is your prayer! So, stand you straight.”\nوَاَغْرَقْتَ فِرعَوْنَ وَقَوْمَهٗ\nWA AGHRAQTA FIR'AWNA WA QAWMAH\nYou thus drowned Pharaoh and his people.\nوَغَفَرْتَ لِدَاوُوْدَ ذَنْبَهٗ\nWA GHAFARTA LIDAAWOODA DHANBAH\nYou forgave the sin of David\nوَتُبْتَ عَلَيْهِ رَحْمَةً مِنْكَ وَذِكْرٰى\nWA TUBTA A'LAYHI RAHMATAN MINKA WA DHIKRAA\nand accepted his repentance out of Your mercy and as a reminder.\nوَفَدَيْتَ اِسْمَاعِيْلَ بِذِبْحٍ عَظِيْمٍ\nWA FADAYTA ISMAA'EELA BIDHIBHIN A'ZEEM\nYou ransomed Ishmael with a momentous sacrifice\nبَعْدَ مَا اَسْلَمَ وَتَلَّهٗ لِلْجَبِيْنِ\nBA'DA MAA ASLAMA WA TALLAHOO LIL JABEEN\nafter he had submitted his will and he had laid him prostrate on his forehead for sacrifice.\nفَنَادَيْتَهٗ بِالْفَرَجِ وَالرَّوْحِ\nFANAADAYTAHOO BIL FARAJI WAR RAWH\nHence, You called him with relief and comfort.\nوَاَنْتَ الَّذِيْ نَادَاكَ زَكَرِيَّا نِدَاءً خَفِيّاً\nWA ANTAL LADHEE NAADAAKA ZAKARIYYAA NIDAA'AN KHAFIYYAA\nAnd it is You to Whom Zachariah cried in secret,\nفَقَالَ رَبِّ اِنِّيْ وَهَنَ الْعَظْمُ مِنِّيْ\nFAQAALA RABBI INNEE WAHANAL A'ZMU MINNEE\npraying, “O my Lord! Infirm indeed are my bones,\nوَاشْتَعَلَ الرَّاْسُ شَيْباً\nWASH TA'ALAR RA'SU SHAYBAA\nand the hair of my head has glistened with grey,\nوَلَمْ اَكُنْ بِدُعَائِكَ رَبِّ شَقِيّاً\nWA LAM AKUN BIDU'AA'IKA RABBI SHAQIYYAA\nbut never am I unblest, O my Lord, in my prayer to You.”\nوَقُلْتَ يَدْعُوْنَنَا رَغَباً وَرَهَباً\nWA QULTA YAD'OONANAA RAGHABAN WA RAHABAA\nAnd You said, “They used to call on Us with love and reverence\nوَكَانُوْا لَنَا خَاشِعِيْنَ\nWA KAANOO LANAA KHAASHI'EEN\nand they humbled themselves before Us.”\nوَاَنْتَ الَّذِيْ اسْتَجَبْتَ لِلَّذِيْنَ آمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوْا الصَّالِحَاتِ\nWA ANTAL LADHEES TAJABTA LILLADHEENA AAMANOO WA A'MILUS SAALIHAAT\nAnd it is You Who responded to those who had believed and done good deeds\nلِتَزِيْدَهُمْ مِنْ فَضْلِكَ\nLITAZEEDAHUM MIN FADLIK\nso as to increase Your favor upon them.\nفَلَا تَجْعَلْنِيْ مِنْ اَهْوَنِ الدَّاعِيْنَ لَكَ وَالرَّاغِبِيْنَ اِلَيْكَ\nFALAA TAJ'ALNEE MIN AHWANID DAA'EENA LAKA WAR RAAGHIBEENA ILAYK\nSo, (please) do not consider me the most debased suppliant and desirous to You.\nوَاسْتَجِبْ لِيْ كَمَا اسْتَجَبْتَ لَهُمْ\nWASTAJIB LEE KAMAS TAJABTA LAHUM\nAnd respond to me in the same way as You responded to them,\nبِحَقِّهِمْ عَلَيْكَ\nBIHAQQIHIM A'LAYK\n(I beseech to You) by their right (that is incumbent) on You.\nفَطَهِّرْنِيْ بِتَطْهِيْـرِكَ\nFATAHHIRNEE BITATHEERIK\nPurify me with Your purification,\nوَتَقَبَّلْ صَلَاتِيْ وَدُعَائِيْ بِقَبُوْلٍ حَسَنٍ\nWA TAQABBAL SALAATEE WA DU'AA'EE BIQABOOLIN HASAN\naccept my prayer and supplication in the best manner,\nوَطَيِّبْ بَقِيَّةَ حَيَاتِيْ\nWA TAYYIB BAQIYYATA HAYAATEE\nmake the rest of my life good,\nوَطَيِّبْ وَفَاتِيْ\nWA TAYYIB WAFAATEE\nmake my demise good,\nوَاخْلُفْنِيْ فِيْمَنْ اَخْلُفُ\nWAKHLUFNEE FEEMAN AKHLUF\nbe the supervisor of my inheritors,\nوَاحْفَظْنِيْ يَا رَبِّ بِدُعَائِيْ\nWAHFAZNEE YAA RABBI BIDU'AA'EE\nsafeguard me, O my Lord, through my supplication,\nوَاجْعَلْ ذُرِّيَّتِيْ ذُرِّيَّةً طَيِّبَةً\nWAJ'AL DHURRIYYATEE DHURRIYYATAN TAYYIBAH\nand make my offspring goodly\nتَحُوْطُهَا بِحِيَاطَتِكَ\nTAHOOTUHAA BIHIYAATATIK\nby encompassing them\nبِكُلِّ مَا حُطْتَ بِهٖ ذُرِّيَّةَ اَحَدٍ مِنْ اَوْلِيَائِكَ وَاَهْلِ طَاعَتِكَ\nBIKULLI MAA HUTTA BIHEE DHURRIYYATA AHADIN MIN AWLIYAA'IKA WA AHLI TAA'ATIK\nwith the same things with which You have encompassed the offspring of Your intimate saints and the people who obeyed You appropriately,\nبِرَحْمَتِكَ يَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nBIRAHMATIKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nout of Your mercy, O most merciful of all those who show mercy.\nيَا مَنْ هُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ رَقِيْبٌ\nYAA MAN HUWA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN RAQEEB\nO You Who observes all things,\nوَلِكُلِّ دَاعٍ مِنْ خَلْقِكَ مُجِيْبٌ\nWA LIKULLI DAA'IN MIN KHALQIKA MUJEEB\nWho answers all those who supplicate to You amongst Your creatures,\nوَمِنْ كُلِّ سَائِلٍ قَرِيْبٌ\nWA MIN KULLI SAA'ILIN QAREEB\nand Who is close to all those who implore You!\nاَسْاَلُكَ يَا لَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ\nAS'ALUKA YAA LAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANT\nI thus implore You, O He save Whom there is no god,\nالْحَيُّ الْقَيُّوْمُ\nAL-HAYYUL QAYYOOM\nO He Who is Ever-living, Self-Subsisting,\nالْاَحَدُ الصَّمَدُ\nAL-AHADUS SAMAD\nOne and Only, Absolute,\nالَّذِيْ لَمْ يَلِدْ وَلَمْ يُوْلَدْ\nALLADHEE LAM YALID WA LAM YOOLAD\nYou beget not nor are You begotten\nوَلَمْ يَكُنْ لَهٗ كُفُواً اَحَدٌ\nWA LAM YAKUN LAHOO KUFUWAN AHAD\nand there is none like unto You.\nوَبِكُلِّ اسْمٍ رَفَعْتَ بِهٖ سَمَاءَكَ\nWA BIKULLIS MIN RAFA'TA BIHEE SAMAA'AK\nAnd I implore You by all Names with which You raised Your heavens,\nوَفَرَشْتَ بِهٖ اَرْضَكَ\nWA FARASHTA BIHEE ARDAK\nspread out Your earth,\nوَاَرْسَيْتَ بِهِ الْجِبَالَ\nWA ARSAYTA BIHIL JIBAAL\nfirmly fixed the mountains,\nوَاَجْرَيْتَ بِهِ الْمَاءَ\nWA AJRAYTA BIHIL MAA'\nmade water flow,\nوَسَخَّرْتَ بِهِ السَّحَابَ\nWA SAKHKHARTA BIHIS SAHAAB\nmade the clouds subservient,\nوَالشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ وَالنُّجُوْمَ\nWASH SHAMSA WAL QAMARA WAN NUJOOM\nas well as the sun, the moon, the stars,\nوَاللَّيْلَ وَالنَّهَارَ\nWAL LAYLA WAN NAHAAR\nthe night, and the daylight,\nوَخَلَقْتَ الْخَلائِقَ كُلَّهَا\nWA KHALAQTAL KHALAA'IQA KULLAHAA\nand created all beings.\nاَسْاَلُكَ بِعَظَمَةِ وَجْهِكَ الْعَظِيْمِ\nAS'ALUKA BI-A'ZAMATI WAJHIKAL A'ZEEM\nI implore You by the magnitude of Your Magnificent Face\nالَّذِيْ اَشْرَقَتْ لَهُ السَّمَاوَاتُ وَالْاَرْضُ\nALLADHEE ASHRAQAT LAHUS SAMAAWAATU WAL ARD\nto which the heavens and the earth shone\nفَاَضَاءَتْ بِهِ الظُّلُمَاتُ\nFA-ADAA'AT BIHIZ ZULUMAAT\ncausing darkness to change into lights,\nاِلَّا صَلَّيْتَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nILLAA SALLAYTA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\n(I implore You by all these) to send blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَكَفَيْتَنِيْ اَمْرَ مَعَاشِيْ وَمَعَادِيْ\nWA KAFAYTANEE AMRA MA'AASHEE WA MA'AADEE\nsave me from the troubles of my living and my other life,\nوَاَصْلَحْتَ لِيْ شَاْنِيْ كُلَّهٗ\nWA ASLAHTA LEE SHA'NEE KULLAH\namend all my affairs,\nوَلَمْ تَكِلْنِيْ اِلٰى نَفْسِيْ طَرْفَةَ عَيْنٍ\nWA LAM TAKILNEE ILAA NAFSEE TARFATA A'YN\nnot to cause me to depend upon myself for even a winking of an eye,\nوَاَصْلَحْتَ اَمْرِيْ وَاَمْرَ عِيَالِيْ\nWA ASLAHTA AMREE WA AMRA I'YAALEE\nmanage the affairs of my household and me,\nوَكَفَيْتَنِيْ هَمَّهُمْ\nWA KAFAYTANEE HAMMAHUM\nsave me from their concerns,\nوَاَغْنَيْتَنِيْ وَاِيَّاهُمْ مِنْ كَنْزِكَ وَخَزَائِنِكَ\nWA AGHNAYTANEE WA IYYAAHUM MIN KANZIKA WA KHAZAA'INIK\nmake them and me rich out of Your treasure, hoards,\nوَسَعَةِ فَضْلِكَ الَّذِيْ لَا يَنْفَدُ اَبَداً\nWA SA'ATI FADLIKAL LADHEE LAA YANFADU ABADAA\nand Your expansive grace that never runs out,\nوَاَثْبِتْ فِيْ قَلْبِيْ يَنَابِيْعَ الْحِكْمَةِ\nWA ATHBIT FEE QALBEE YANAABEE'AL HIKMAH\nfix in my heart founts of sagacity\nالَّتِيْ تَنْفَعُنِيْ بِهَا\nALLATEE TANFA'UNEE BIHAA\nfrom which I may benefit\nوَتَنْفَعُ بِهَا مَنِ ارْتَضَيْتَ مِنْ عِبَادِكَ\nWA TANFA'U BIHAA MANIR TADAYTA MIN I'BAADIK\nand from which You may benefit Your servants with whom You are pleased,\nوَاجْعَلْ لِيْ مِنَ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ\nWAJ'AL LEE MINAL MUTTAQEEN\nand make me, from among the pious,\nفِيْ آخِرِ الزَّمَانِ اِمَاماً\nFEE AAKHIRIZ ZAMAANI IMAAMAA\na leader (imam) in the last of times,\nكَمَا جَعَلْتَ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ الْخَلِيْلَ اِمَاماً\nKAMAA JA'ALTA IBRAAHEEMAL KHALEELA IMAAMAA\nin the same way as You made Abraham Your intimate friend to be a leader.\nفَاِنَّ بِتَوْفِيْقِكَ يَفُوْزُ الْفَائِزُوْنَ\nFA-INNA BITAWFEEQIKA YAFOOZUL FAA'IZOON\nVerily, only through Your guidance do the winners achieve prosperity,\nوَيَتُوْبُ التَّائِبُوْنَ\nWA YATOOBUT TAA'IBOON\nthe repentant declare repentance,\nوَيَعْبُدُكَ الْعَابِدُوْنَ\nWA YA'BUDUKAL A'ABIDOON\nand the true worshippers worship You.\nوَبِتَسْدِيْدِكَ يَصْلُحُ الصَّالِحُوْنَ\nWA BITASDEEDIKA YASLUHUS SAALIHOON\nAnd only through Your supervision do the righteous,\nالْمُحْسِنُوْنَ الْمُخْبِتُوْنَ\nAL-MUHSINOONAL MUKHBITOON\nthe good-doers, those who humble themselves before You,\nالْعَابِدُوْنَ لَكَ الْخَائِفُوْنَ مِنْكَ\nAL-A'ABIDOONA LAKAL KHAA'IFOONA MINK\nthose who worship You sincerely, and those who fear You become righteous.\nوَبِاِرْشَادِكَ نَجَا النَّاجُوْنَ مِنْ نَارِكَ\nWA BI-IRSHAADIKA NAJAN NAAJOONA MIN NAARIK\nAnd only through Your direction will those who will be delivered from Your Hellfire be saved\nوَاَشْفَقَ مِنْهَا الْمُشْفِقُوْنَ مِنْ خَلْقِكَ\nWA ASHFAQA MINHAL MUSHFIQOONA MIN KHALQIK\nand those who fear You, from amongst Your creatures, stand in awe of it.\nوَبِخِذْلَانِكَ خَسِرَ الْمُبْطِلُوْنَ\nWA BIKHIDHLAANIKA KHASIRAL MUBTILOON\nBut through Your disappointing them will the wrong lose,\nوَهَلَكَ الظَّالِمُوْنَ\nWA HALAKAZ ZAALIMOON\nthe unjust perish,\nوَغَفَلَ الْغَافِلُوْنَ\nWA GHAFALAL GHAAFILOON\nand those distracted from You be inattentive.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ آتِ نَفْسِيْ تَقْوَاهَا\nALLAAHUMMA AATI NAFSEE TAQWAAHAA\nO Allah, grant my soul its piety\nفَاَنْتَ وَلِيُّهَا وَمَوْلَاهَا\nFA-ANTA WALIYYUHAA WA MAWLAAHAA\nfor You are its guardian and master\nوَاَنْتَ خَيْرُ مَنْ زَكَّاهَا\nWA ANTA KHAYRU MAN ZAKKAAHAA\nand You are the best to purify it.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ بَيِّنْ لَهَا هُدَاهَا\nALLAAHUMMA BAYYIN LAHAA HUDAAHAA\nO Allah, show it its true guidance,\nوَاَلْهِمْهَا تَقْوَاهَا\nWA ALHIMHAA TAQWAAHAA\ninspire it with what is good for it,\nوَبَشِّرْهَا بِرَحْمَتِكَ حِيْنَ تَتَوَفَّاهَا\nWA BASHSHIRHAA BIRAHMATIKA HEENA TATAWAFFAAHAA\ncarry to it the good news of Your mercy when You grasp it,\nوَنَزِّلْهَا مِنَ الْجِنَانِ عُلْيَاهَا\nWA NAZZILHAA MINAL JINAANI U'LYAAHAA\nlodge it in the highest positions of the gardens of Paradise,\nوَطَيِّبْ وَفَاتَهَا وَمَحْيَاهَا\nWA TAYYIB WAFAATAHAA WA MAHYAAHAA\nmake good its death and life,\nوَاَكْرِمْ مُنْقَلَبَهَا وَمَثْوَاهَا\nWA AKRIM MUNQALABAHAA WA MATHWAAHAA\nand honor its place and abode\nوَمُسْتَقَرَّهَا وَمَاْوَاهَا\nWA MUSTAQARRAHAA WA MA'WAAHAA\nand its dwelling and house,\nفَاَنْتَ وَلِيُّهَا وَمَوْلَاهَا\nFA-ANTA WALIYYUHAA WA MAWLAAHAA\nfor You are its guardian and master.",
  "merits": "In his book of Jamal al-Usbu', Sayyid Ibn Tawus has recorded a special prayer and supplication for each of the Holy Imams (a.s.), to be offered on Fridays.\nThis prayer consists of four units in each of which [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) are repeated twenty-five times. While genuflecting, [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) are repeated ten times. So is done when one raises his head after the genuflection (ruku') and while prostrating oneself and between the two prostrations."
}
